course: dictionary
lesson: 5067
title: Instalment: one part at a time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An instalment is one part of something that is paid or given in pieces, one at a time. Look at the clue words in this sentence: «Buy now pay later splits a purchase into instalments; it is still borrowing, with charges if a payment is late.» The purchase is split into pieces, so an instalment must be one of those pieces.
explain: The second meaning is about stories. «Did you read the next instalment of the comic?» The clue words are comic and next. A comic story can come out bit by bit, one part after another, so an instalment is one part of that story. Ask yourself what word would fit: part, episode, chapter.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The bike was paid for in 6 instalments.» Does "paid for in 6 parts over time" make sense? Yes. Does "paid for in one lump sum" make sense? No, so the word means parts, not the whole.
fact: An instalment is one of several parts of something, paid or given at different times.
fact: In American English the spelling is «installment», with a double l.
fact: «Buy now pay later splits a price into instalments, like £400 as 10 × £40.» Each instalment here is £40.
fact: An instalment plan is still borrowing, and a late payment can bring extra charges.
fact: A series is a set of stories or programmes that come out one after another, and each new part is an instalment.
exercise: «Buy now pay later splits a price into instalments, like £400 as 10 × £40.» How much is each instalment? | £10 | *£40 | £410 | £400
exercise: A £60 bike is paid for in 3 equal instalments. How much is each instalment? | £30 | £3 | *£20 | £180
exercise: «Did you read the next instalment of the comic?» What does instalment mean here? | *A new part of the story, coming out bit by bit | A bag of crisps | A receipt from the shop | A cover drawn in colour
test: Which spelling is the American one for instalment? | installement | instalment | *installment | instalement
test: «It is still borrowing, with charges if a payment is late.» What can happen if an instalment is late? | Nothing ever happens | The price goes down | *Extra charges may be added | You get a prize from the shop
exam: Jayden buys a £300 bike and pays it off in 6 equal instalments. How much is each instalment? | £30 | £300 | *£50 | £60
